  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the dehumanizing textual metaphor",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'this is the worst cancer i've ever seen', which functions as a deictic statement directed at the viewer. The phrase 'I've ever seen' implies the user is the one making the judgment, thereby projecting the user's identity onto the act of dehumanization. The user is not explicitly addressed with 'you' or 'your', but the first-person pronoun 'I' in 'I've seen' creates a direct projection of the user's perspective and moral judgment onto the visual entity (the flag of Israel) and the antisemitic metaphor it represents.",
